{{prime disambiguation|Rom}}

'''Rom''' was a [[Ferengi]] [[mercenary]] in the [[mirror universe]]. He fought in the [[Terran Resistance Forces]] during the [[Terran Rebellion]] against the [[Klingon-Cardassian Alliance]], seeking revenge against the Alliance for the death of his elder [[brother]], {{mu|Quark}}. Compared to [[Rom|his primary universe counterpart]], Rom was much more aggressive and devious.

As part of a plan to get [[Benjamin Sisko]] aboard {{mu|Terok Nor}}, Rom pretended to defect to the Alliance and revealed that Sisko, who had been believed dead, was planning to come to the station. The Alliance, using Rom's information, managed to capture Sisko and {{mu|Miles O'Brien|"Smiley" O'Brien}}, and bring them to the station, which was exactly what the rebels wanted. Rom was to pilot their escape ship once Sisko and Smiley had rescued {{mu|Jennifer Sisko}} from the Alliance.

Unfortunately, {{mu|Elim Garak}} was suspicious of Rom and ordered him [[torture]]d into revealing the true plan. Rom was then [[execute]]d, and his body was left impaled upon an [[airlock]] door as a warning. ({{DS9|Through the Looking Glass}})

After his [[death]], {{mu|Quark's|his late brother's bar}} on Terok Nor was inherited by his son {{mu|Nog}}, who was killed by [[Intendant]] {{mu|Kira Nerys}} in [[2372]]. ({{DS9|Shattered Mirror}})

Upon visiting the mirror universe in [[2375]], the Rom of the primary universe expressed sadness at the death of his counterpart. He told his brother [[Quark]] that he would have liked to have met himself. ({{DS9|The Emperor's New Cloak}})

{{bginfo|Like [[Rom|his prime counterpart]], Rom was portrayed by [[Max Grodénchik]].|In the script of "Through the Looking Glass" (both the first draft and final draft), the alternate Rom was described as "a hardened, heavily armed professional soldier." ''{{Star Trek Minutiae|resources/scripts/466.txt}}'' Grodénchik described the character as "tough, hotheaded and bloodthirsty for revenge." ''{{el|articles.philly.com/1995-02-21/news/25705911_1_quark-armin-shimerman-ferengi}}''}}

